--- frontend/src/renderer/components/chat/ChatComposer.tsx:701 ---
👮 **Wachiman** · 🟠🐛 **Fix · bug: Ordinary optimistic sends no longer take files for the next message, contrary to "unchanged" (confidence medium)**

`takesNextFiles = optimisticSend && restoring` now replaces bare `optimisticSend` in `attachBlocked`, `acceptsFiles`, `onDragOver`, the chip remove handler, the file input and the Add trigger. On main, any optimistic send (`durableDelivery.draft && composerMutation.pending`) accepted paste, drop and picker for the next message. The old tests in this file proved it: they rendered `<ChatComposer>` without `restoring` and asserted the attach button was enabled. This PR adds `restoring` to all of them. A new test (line 356) asserts that an ordinary send takes no file. `restoring` is only true for an archived chat's restore (`ChatWorkspace.tsx:1080`). So paste, drop and picker are now refused during every ordinary send, where main took them. The PR body says "Ordinary sends, New Chat and archived Cloud chats are unchanged". If narrowing is intended, say so in the body. Otherwise use `optimisticSend || restoring`-style gating that keeps the old behaviour for ordinary sends. Nothing is shown when a paste is refused, so the pasted file is dropped silently.

<!-- wachi:finding -->
--- frontend/src/renderer/components/chat/ChatComposer.tsx:701 ---
👮 **Wachiman** · 🟡📝 **Consider · docs: PR body says next files are taken only when the sent message has no files; the code and tests do the opposite (confidence medium)**

The body says the composer takes next files "only when the message being sent has no files of its own", and that when the restoring message has files "attaching stays closed until it lands, as on main". `takesNextFiles` (this line) never looks at `durableDelivery.draft.attachments`. The tests at `ChatComposer.optimistic.test.tsx:214-235` and `:258-280` send a message that has files (`sent.png`, or eight sent files) and still expect `next.png` to be accepted while `restoring` is set. Correct the body, or add the check the body describes. The "Coverage and risks" section is the part a reviewer relies on.

