--- frontend/src/renderer/hooks/useRestoreSession.ts:143 ---
👮 **Wachiman** · 🟡🐛 **Consider · bug: A second restore for the same session still POSTs to the daemon and hands the caller its refusal (confidence low)**

The fix keeps the first promise in `restoresInFlight`, which is right. A second call still runs `restoreSession`, which POSTs `/restore` again (the test pins `[RESTORE, RESTORE]`). The daemon answers `SESSION_OPERATION_IN_PROGRESS` (`backend/internal/service/session/service.go:2150`) and the caller gets `{status:"error"}` for a restore that is actually progressing. The cloud branch's comment at line 77 says a second ask joins the one in flight. Returning the in-flight promise for the local path would do the same and avoid the spurious error. Check first what the other callers do with an `error` result. A related nit: the test mock (`useConversation.test.tsx:1751`) uses code `OPERATION_IN_PROGRESS`, but the daemon's code is `SESSION_OPERATION_IN_PROGRESS`.

<!-- wachi:finding -->
--- frontend/src/renderer/components/chat/ChatComposer.tsx:2292 ---
👮 **Wachiman** · 🟡🐛 **Consider · bug: A held Enter is dropped without notice when the next draft's files change before the send lands (confidence medium)**

A held message is now sent only if `heldSubmit.files === nextFilesKey()`. The key is the sorted ids of the staged and pending files. If the user holds Enter (text only, or with files) and then adds or removes a file during the restore, the held message is never sent. It is also not queued or flagged, and the text stays in the box. The new test at `ChatComposer.optimistic.test.tsx:331` covers removing a file and adding another. The other direction is not covered: Enter on text alone, then a paste to go with it. That drops the Enter too. If this is intended, consider a visible hint, or compare only the files that were present at Enter.

